<div class="source-doc-poem">
  <p>Oh Lord, how I loved those lofty heights<br>
  where I followed the alteration<br>
  that turned hard rock soft from dissolved pyrites<br>
  in a subtle form of creation</p>

  <p>There's a pluton buried beneath my feet<br>
  I smell it under Cascade Mountain<br>
  a seething mass that provided the heat<br>
  and the minerals to ascend like a fountain</p>

  <p>Healing the breccia of a volcano's death throes<br>
  filling the cracks from it's spasms<br>
  providing the smells for a prospector's nose<br>
  as he works his way up rocky chasms</p>

  <p>I've covered the ground where clear streams head<br>
  and panned gravel beds at their end<br>
  staked out my placer but found, instead<br>
  the gold was around the next bend</p>

  <p>And now I know where the bonanza lies<br>
  the Lord led me to this great stope<br>
  a golden horizon that dazzles my eyes<br>
  in a sunrise with promise and hope</p>
