<section class="source-doc-transcript">
  <h2 id="acknowledgements">Acknowledgements</h2>

  <p>In the first publication we gave credit to several persons who played a part in the effort through encouragement, contributions of photos and memories, or because of associations that improved and enriched the author's life.</p>

  <p>With the possibility that <em>Who Upset the Thundermug</em>, a sequel to <em>Once Around the Thundermug</em>, may enter book-stores several of my friends have pleaded with me, "We like you, John Jackson, but please, please don't list our names in acknowledgements."</p>

  <p>In respect to those dear friends I will dedicate <em>Who Upset the Thundermug to</em> my beloved sister, <a href="/people/alice-josephine-davis/#pauline-roberta-jackson-bates">Pauline Roberta Jackson Bates</a>, who was embarrassed unto tears so many times as I was trying to find myself. One of her most vivid embarrassments was the time the town Marshal found me before I could find myself. I fear this publication may be another embarrassment.</p>

  <p>I would also like to dedicate this collection of humorous stories to my good friends and co-workers, Lynn "Key" Lezotte and Monte Jay Larson who left us several years ago. They were among our most productive citizens and inspired us all.</p>

  <p>Special thanks to H. Heinie Leonard for critique and encouragement. To Gordon and Cloy Duncan who contributed several photographs.</p>

  <p class="source-doc-note"><em>"Lezotte" is spelled this way here and "LeZotte" in the story "The Con Boss Conned"; both are kept as printed. The book's photographs of Key and Monte Jay Larson appear on the Chapter I page, beside the stories where they are pictured.</em></p>

  <p class="source-doc-note"><em>"Once Around the Thunder Mug" carries its own Acknowledgements, in which John thanks Heinie and Vivian Leonard and Gordon and Cloy Duncan by name. See <a href="/writings/once-around-the-thunder-mug/#acknowledgments">that page</a>.</em></p>
</section>

